<title>CANADA: Derlan gets C$25.3 mln Boeing deal.</title>
<headline>Derlan gets C$25.3 mln Boeing deal.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Derlan Industries Ltd said on Monday its Derlan Aerospace Canada division signed a memorandum of agreement valued at C$25.3 million with Boeing Co's helicopter division to manufacture transmission components for the Boeing CH46 helicopter.</p>
<p>Delivery was expected to begin in early 1997 and continue through 1999, Derlan said.</p>
<p>It said the contract called for Derlan to supply Boeing helicopter with more than 1,900 various gears and gear assemblies for the CH46, used by the U.S. Navy and Marines.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau  (416) 941-8100</p>
